be as the grass of the housetops, which withers before it is plucked up.","poem":1}]},{"type":"verse","number":7,"content":[{"lineBreak":true},{"text":"Wherewith the reaper fills not his hand, nor he that makes up the sheaves, his bosom.","poem":1}]},{"type":"verse","number":8,"content":[{"lineBreak":true},{"text":"Neither do they that go by say, The blessing of the Lord be upon you: we have blessed you in the name of the Lord.","poem":1}]}],"footnotes":[{"noteId":233,"caller":"+","text":"שיך iniquity, easily read for שוכה a furrow.","reference":{"chapter":128,"verse":3}}]},"thisChapterLink":"/api/eng_lxx/PSA/128.json","thisChapterAudioLinks":{},"nextChapterApiLink":"/api/eng_lxx/PSA/129.json","nextChapterAudioLinks":{},"previousChapterApiLink":"/api/eng_lxx/PSA/127.json","previousChapterAudioLinks":{},"numberOfVerses":8}